<.shell current={:toast}>
  <h1>Toast</h1>
  <p class="lead">The result of what the person did. It comes and goes.</p>

  <div class="demo">
    <div class="toasts">
      <.flash id="sample-flash-info" kind={:info}>4 attendance changes sent.</.flash>
      <.flash id="sample-flash-info-sub" kind={:info} title="ID cards saved.">
        Cards on members' phones update in about a minute.
      </.flash>
      <.flash id="sample-flash-error" kind={:error} title="D4H refused the change">
        Nothing changed. Check the access key in team settings.
      </.flash>
      <.flash id="sample-flash-new-version" kind={:info} title="SAR Duty has a new version">
        <.a href="#">Reload this page</.a> to use it.
      </.flash>
      <.flash id="sample-flash-disconnected" kind={:error} title="Server disconnected">
        Reconnecting… <.spinner />
      </.flash>
    </div>
  </div>
  <.form_actions>
    <.button data-toast="info">Show an info toast</.button>
    <.button data-toast="error">Show an error toast</.button>
  </.form_actions>
  <div class="toasts" id="toasts" aria-live="polite"></div>
  <template id="toast-info">
    <.flash id="sample-toast-info" kind={:info}>Settings saved.</.flash>
  </template>
  <template id="toast-error">
    <.flash id="sample-toast-error" kind={:error} title="Letter not created">
      Enter who authorizes tax letters in team settings.
    </.flash>
  </template>
  <script>
    document.querySelectorAll("[data-toast]").forEach(function (button) {
      button.addEventListener("click", function () {
        var kind = button.dataset.toast;
        var toast = document.getElementById("toast-" + kind).content.firstElementChild.cloneNode(true);
        toast.removeAttribute("id");
        document.getElementById("toasts").appendChild(toast);
        toast.addEventListener("click", function () { toast.remove(); });
        if (kind !== "error") setTimeout(function () { toast.remove(); }, 6000);
      });
    });
  </script>

  <h2>When to use</h2>
  <ul>
    <li>A result toast says what the person's action did.</li>
    <li>
      An error toast is for an action that failed. The first sentence says what went wrong, the
      next what to do.
    </li>
    <li>
      A page open since a deploy says SAR Duty has a new version, with a link to reload it.
    </li>
  </ul>

  <h2>When not to use</h2>
  <p>
    Never put the only copy of important information in a toast. Use a <a href={
      page_path(:banner)
    }>banner</a>.
  </p>

  <h2>How it works</h2>
  <ul>
    <li>
      One pill, centred under the top bar on every screen, clear of the page's buttons. A new
      message takes its place.
    </li>
    <li>
      A result is the theme turned inside out: dark on the light theme, light on the dark one.
      An error is red. The first sentence is the title, the rest the subtitle.
    </li>
    <li>
      A result fades after 6 seconds, or 10 with a subtitle. The clock stops while the pointer,
      a finger, or focus is on it, or the person is in another app or tab.
    </li>
    <li>An error stays until it is closed, replaced, or the person goes to another page.</li>
    <li>× or a tap anywhere on the toast closes it.</li>
    <li>
      The Server disconnected toast shows while LiveView reconnects and goes when it is back.
    </li>
  </ul>

  <h2>In the app</h2>
  <p>
    LiveView's flash: <code>put_flash(socket, :info, "…")</code>. The layout's
    <code>&lt;.flash_group&gt;</code>
    shows them with <code>&lt;.flash&gt;</code>.
  </p>
</.shell>
